 "content": "# Noisy motif translations\n\nUse this branch when a distinctive single-color motif appears amid zeros and another background color, and the grid may contain translated copies of that seed. Record the colored-cell offsets relative to the motif's bounding box; search legal translations whose corresponding positions are all zero, and recolor only those matching positions with the motif color. Preserve every other cell, including the original motif and zeros/background at non-motif positions inside the bounding box. Do not substitute flood-fill or neighbor propagation. Account for the seed shape and grid bounds; consider rotation or reflection only when demonstrations support it. Check each proposed change and non-change against every demonstration.\n"
}

