 "path": "continual-arc/references/separator-tile-mapping.md",
 "content": "# Separator tile mapping\n\nUse this branch when full-width and full-height separator lines divide the grid into equal tiles and the output dimensions match the tile layout. Map each tile to one output cell, then use demonstrations to identify the in-tile feature or count that determines that cell; do not assume every unusual cell or a single marker is positive. For the observed pattern with color-8 separators and 2×3 tiles containing mostly color 3 with occasional color 2, output 1 when a tile has at least two 2s, and 3 otherwise. Verify the rule against all demonstrated tiles before applying it to the full grid.\n"
}

{
 "path": "continual-arc/references/diagonal-stripe-phases.md",
 "content": "# Diagonal stripe phases\n\nUse this branch when sparse colored diagonal markers on a zero field may define periodic stripes that fill the output. For down-right diagonals, the invariant is constant row−column and, with zero-based coordinates, `column−row` indexes the stripe phase; for down-left diagonals, the invariant and phase index are `row+column`. Verify the orientation and sign against observed outputs. Infer the smallest plausible period whose residues do not require conflicting colors, and use demonstrations to establish the complete phase-to-color mapping. Color every cell from its phase rather than preserving only the markers. Check multiple cells on each demonstrated line and reproduce every demo; marker positions alone may not reveal all residues.\n"
}

{
 "path": "continual-arc/references/edge-continuation.md",
 "content": "# Edge continuation\n\nUse this branch when demonstrations show color 1 marking an absent continuation at a grid edge among repeated rows, bands, or motif copies. Compare the repetitions to infer both the expected continuation and affected cells; it may be a solid suffix or only selected motif-phase positions. Color only confirmed missing continuation cells, preserving the existing motif and unrelated cells. Choose repeated copies from the demonstration evidence, not from rightmost zeros or suffix length alone, and verify every changed and unchanged cell against all demos.\n"
}
